e too far from what I have in mind.  I am not sure that Hans' paper will he=
lp you much, for, while I taken over some things from him in terms of dynam=
ic domains and alternate domains, I have developed somewhat differently, as=
 Lojban seems to require.
Particular quantification is the old term for existential quantification, w=
ith the advantage that it does not appear to claim more than something is i=
n the domain, in particular, does not appear to claim it is the extension o=
f "exist" {zasti}.
Sorry about the mumble there; I am just never sure which procedure works be=
st: a supply of things that turn up in different guises in each world or a =
different set of things for each world, somehow sometimes linked between wo=
rlds.  Neither is perfect, but each has it's uses. (Hindu v. Buddhist, as s=
o many things are).
